# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Line endings — keep Linux scripts LF on EVERY platform, including Windows.
#
#  Why this file exists (do not remove):
#  These shell scripts run directly on Linux / WSL / SteamOS, and are often
#  shared as raw files (e.g. posted to Discord) and run straight from the
#  download. Git's core.autocrlf=true converts text to CRLF on a Windows
#  checkout, which turns the shebang into `#!/bin/bash<CR>`. Linux then fails
#  to run the script with:
#        cannot execute: required file not found
#  because it looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/bash\r".
#
#  `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree regardless of OS or autocrlf, so
#  editing the source on Windows can never reintroduce CRLF into a script.
#  (Future extensionless scripts — e.g. a launcher with no .sh — must be
#  added here explicitly by path, since these globs match by extension.)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.zsh   text eol=lf
*.ksh   text eol=lf
*.fish  text eol=lf
*.bats  text eol=lf

# Our Eluna bridge scripts only (deployed straight to the Linux AC server's
# lua_scripts dir). Scoped deliberately: a repo-wide *.lua rule would rewrite
# the CRLF-carrying pristine upstream reference copies under guides/.
cli/lua/**/*.lua text eol=lf

# Extensionless built CLI artifact (bash script, no .sh suffix) — see note above.
cli/dml text eol=lf

# Extensionless placeholder for the CI-built Linux dml-wow binary (real
# releases overwrite it with an ELF; keep the placeholder's own #!/bin/sh
# header LF so a stray direct run under WSL bash doesn't choke on CRLF).
launcher/src-tauri/backend/dml-wow text eol=lf

# Test fixtures parsed byte-for-byte by CLI code (e.g. the server-info SOAP
# parser splits on LF): a CRLF-injected checkout on an autocrlf=true box
# would corrupt these and break the tests they feed.
cli/tests/fixtures/*.txt text eol=lf
cli/tests/fixtures/*.xml text eol=lf
cli/tests/fixtures/*.tsv text eol=lf

# Static registry snapshots embedded via include_str! in dml-wow — generated
# from the bash `dml` oracle in WSL (LF-native); keep LF on Windows checkouts
# so the committed blob and working tree byte-match regardless of autocrlf.
crates/dml-wow/data/*.json text eol=lf

# The migration stack's compose is COPIED VERBATIM into the runtime title dir
# and read by docker compose against the Linux VM; check-migrate-scripts.sh
# asserts it carries no CR bytes, so pin it here rather than leaving that
# assertion at the mercy of core.autocrlf. Scoped to this dir on purpose — a
# repo-wide *.yml rule would rewrite unrelated upstream YAML.
poc/native-docker/migrate/*.yml text eol=lf

# Compose templates embedded via include_str! in dml-wow's composegen — their
# bytes ARE the docker-compose files a native install writes out. Keep LF so a
# Windows checkout can't hand the Linux containers CRLF YAML.
crates/dml-wow/data/*.tmpl text eol=lf

# The Wrath Unbound add-on payload: C++, SQL, Lua and a git patch extracted
# byte-for-byte from install-wrath-unbound-addon.sh and embedded via
# include_str!. RECURSIVE on purpose — the `data/*.json` and `data/*.tmpl`
# globs above do NOT reach a subdirectory, and this tree is three levels deep.
#
# The patch is why this matters more here than anywhere else in the repo:
# `git apply` compares context lines EXACTLY, and six of them are a single
# space (unified-diff context for blank source lines). A CRLF checkout turns
# each into " \r" and the patch stops applying — against a server the user
# already plays on, mid-rebuild. Nothing else in the run would report a cause.
crates/dml-wow/data/unbound/** text eol=lf

# The Wrath Unbound CLIENT addons: vendored third-party files this repo never
# edits, embedded with include_bytes! and pinned by an FNV fingerprint.
#
# BINARY for the WHOLE tree, deliberately. Five files are .blp (WoW's texture
# format) and would be corrupted outright by EOL conversion -- but the Lua is
# marked binary too, because the pin is over BYTES and must not depend on
# whether a given checkout normalised line endings. Readable diffs are worth
# less here than a payload that is identical on every machine.
crates/dml-wow/data/unbound-addons/** -text
